   "text": "The four jobs of a manager. Being a manager is not a title; it is four jobs you do every week. Job one: get the work done. Job two: take care of your people. Job three: make things better. Job four: connect your team to the rest of Vanderbilt. Every manager does all four, and most weeks need one more than the others. Part of the job is noticing which. Tap each card on the page to see the habits inside."
